  "tests": [
    "CP01-1: SHA-256 repositories export verifiable objects without the source",
    "CP01-1: input pins are captured before awaits and manifest contradictions are rejected",
    "CP01-2: source changes after staging starts abort publication and preserve the source",
    "CP01-2: ancestor symlinks, hidden dirty index flags, and promisor markers fail closed",
    "CP01-1: uncompressed and duration budgets abort without publishing or editing the source",
    "CP01-2: an unconfigured LFS pointer anywhere in selected history rejects incomplete content",
    "CP02-1: Git restore rebinds selected IDs and ordered roles after source and backup deletion",
    "CP02-2: forged, stale and mismatched Git restore handles cannot produce bindings",
    "CP02-2: binding inputs are captured, unselected workspaces stay intact, and branch mode is explicit",
    "CP02-2: restored binding uses the existing checkout guard and holds stale HEAD before an owner action",
    "CP02-1: multiple worktrees retain separate explicit workspace roots and representation identities",
    "CP01-1: standalone CLI exports an explicitly pinned clean repository",
    "CP01-2: Git export CLI refuses invalid flags, special files, and spec destinations",
    "CP02-1: standalone import CLI restores native Git data without source or original backup",
    "CP02-2: import CLI refuses spec-selected destinations, unsafe spec files and unknown flags",
    "CP02-1: restores independently from copied transport after original common store disappears",
    "CP02-2: serializes a destination reservation and preserves an existing destination",
    "CP02-2: rejects tampered receipt, collisions, traversal and duplicate native revision before destination publication",
    "CP02-1: SHA-256 restores complete trees, executable bits and independent object storage",
    "CP02-2: failed file pins and aggregate checkout budgets clean only newly reserved destinations",
    "CP02-2: receipt metadata and a corrupted pack cannot inherit a valid-looking digest chain",
    "CP02-2: unsupported transformations, case collisions and symlink transports are refused",
    "CP02-2: captured inputs, branch collisions and ignored additions cannot bypass verification",
    "CP03-1: working deletion, executable mode divergence, detached worktree and index v4 stay distinct",
    "CP03-1: binary state above four MiB verifies within an explicit budget without disclosing unselected bytes",
    "CP03-2: intent-to-add, assume flags, attributes, LFS and special selections HOLD without publication",
    "CP03-2: state changes during capture and exhausted budgets leave no artifact or source edits",
    "CP03-2: rehashed receipts cannot validate missing blobs, incorrect native OIDs, mixed stages or broader scope",
    "CP03-2: path collisions, stale independent pins and input mutation cannot broaden selected capture",
    "CP03-1: restored dirty bytes rebind stable resource IDs and ordered roles with a distinct state revision",
    "CP03-1: multi-worktree restores keep staged deletion, working deletion, rename and detached state separate",
    "CP03-2: stale, serialized, cross-profile and wrong-revision handles cannot update a binding",
    "CP03-2: state and history mismatches fail before publication even with a fully rehashed receipt",
    "CP03-2: budgets and explicit selection pins prevent partial or misidentified state restores",
    "CP03-2: one destination reservation wins, existing data remains intact and metadata edits stale the restore",
    "CP03-2: internal overlay integrity cannot mint a verified CP03 state or clean binding handle",
    "CP03-1: restores a copied state sidecar onto the clean bundle's exact native index and dirty working bytes",
    "CP03-1: restores SHA-256 conflict stages and executable working mode without treating the handle as serializable",
    "CP03-1: captures staged A/worktree B, deletion, rename, executable mode, and selected binary/empty untracked bytes",
    "CP03-1: copied artifact verifies after source and original backup are deleted, with no restore authority",
    "CP03-1: captures SHA-256 object IDs and native conflict stages which round-trip into an isolated Git index",
    "CP03-2: rejects unsafe Git states, selected paths, unsupported index flags, and incomplete operations",
    "CP03-2: edited state bytes cannot inherit the original receipt pin",
    "CP03-2: verifier rejects wrong identity/head and an altered receipt",
    "CP01-1: exports a clean detached linked worktree as a native self-contained bundle without source paths",
    "CP01-1: rejects independently pinned HEAD/ref/object-format disagreement before publishing",
    "CP01-2: rejects dirty index, worktree, and untracked states without changing the source",
    "CP01-2: rejects unsupported repository closure forms without executing configured filters",
    "CP01-1: rejects shallow and alternates repositories rather than borrowing an original object store",
    "CP01-1: refuses symlink roots, malformed refs, accessors, and tiny budgets without publication",
    "CP01-2: rejects unborn and LFS/filter worktrees before publication or filter execution"
  ],
